lesson: 162
title: Dividing bigger numbers in stories
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dividing tells how many equal groups there are, or how many go into each group, when the total is large.
explain: 816 eggs in trays of 24: 24 × 30 = 720 leaves 96, and 96 = 24 × 4, so there are 30 + 4 = 34 trays.
explain: Check by multiplying back: 34 × 24 = 816.
vars: a=name k=12..25 q=11..40 x=2..9
need: q * k <= 1000
answer: q
exercise: A farm packs {q*k} eggs into trays of {k}. How many trays does it fill?
exercise: {q*k} children go on a trip in buses. Each bus takes {k} children. How many buses are needed?
exercise: {k} classes share {q*k} books equally. How many books does each class get?
exercise: A book has {q*k} pages. {a} reads {k} pages a day. How many days does it take {a.him} to read the book?
exercise: {q*k} chairs stand in {k} equal rows. How many chairs are in each row?
exercise: A rope {q*k} cm long is cut into pieces of {k} cm. How many pieces are there?
test: How many boxes of {k} cans each can be filled from {q*k} cans?
test: A factory made {q*k} toys in {k} days, the same number each day. How many toys did it make in one day?
test: {a} saved {q*k} dollars by putting away {k} dollars every week. How many weeks did {a.he} save for?
test: There are {q*k} seats in a cinema, arranged in rows of {k}. The cinema has {x} doors. How many rows of seats are there?
exercise: A school in Ohio has {q*k} pupils and puts {k} pupils in each class. How many classes are there?
exercise: How many bags are needed for {q*k} oranges if each bag holds {k} oranges?
exercise: {a} shares {q*k} stickers equally among {k} friends. How many stickers does every friend get?
exercise: A farmer in Kent packs {q*k} apples into boxes of {k} apples apiece. How many boxes does he fill?
exercise: {q*k} dollars are split equally between {k} children. How many dollars does each child receive?
exercise: A ferry in Vancouver carries {k} cars per trip. How many trips does it take to carry {q*k} cars?
exercise: {a} saves the same amount every week and has {q*k} dollars after {k.words} weeks. How many dollars does {a.he} save per week?
exercise: A gardener in Christchurch plants {q*k} tulips in {k} equal rows. How many tulips go in every row?
test: {k} buses take {q*k} fans to a match in Glasgow, each bus carrying the same number. How many fans ride in one bus?
test: What is the number of teams if {q*k} players in a league in Texas are split into teams of {k}?
test: A library in Perth spreads {q*k} new books evenly over {k} shelves. How many books does one shelf get?
test: {a} has a ribbon {q*k} cm long and snips it into equal lengths of {k} cm. How many lengths does {a.he} get?
test: {q*k} biscuits are put into packets, {k} to a packet, at a factory with {x} machines. How many packets are filled?
test: Walking {k} km every day, how many days does it take {a} to walk {q*k} km along a trail in Ireland?
exercise: {q*k} eggs, trays of {k}, how many trays
exercise: {q*k} kids going on the trip, {k} a bus, how many buses we need
exercise: share {q*k} stickers between {k+1} mates — no wait, {k} mates. how many each
exercise: Sam says {q*k} take away {k} is {q*k-k} books a class. nah that's wrong. {k} classes share {q*k} books equal, how many each
test: rope's {q*k} cm, cut in bits of {k} cm, how many bits u get
test: saved {k} dollar a week, got {q*k} now, oh and spent {x} on sweets but that was birthday money. how many weeks i been saving
test: {a} reckons {q*k} seats in rows of {k} is {q+k} rows. wrong innit? how many rows really
exercise: Great-aunt May passed on and left {q*k} dollars to be shared equally between her {k} grandchildren. How many dollars does each grandchild get?
exercise: old dog was put down so we've got {q*k} cans of dog food going spare. bloody hell, pack 'em in boxes of {k} for the shelter. how many boxes
test: Mum is between jobs, so the family has to make {q*k} dollars last {k} weeks. If they spend the same every week, how many dollars can they spend each week?
exam: It is given that {q*k} eggs are packed into trays, each tray containing {k} eggs. Determine the number of trays thereby filled.
exam: Whereas {q*k} children are to be conveyed in buses, each bus carrying {k} children, ascertain the number of buses required.
exam: Ascertain the quotient obtained upon the division of {q*k} by {k}.
exam: A sum of {q*k} dollars is distributed in equal shares of {k} dollars each. State the number of shares so formed.
